; M1941 Johnson light machine gun, assembled from primitives.
; Local space matches the other weapons: barrel fires along -Z, +Y up. Roughly
; life-size (~1.07m long).
;
; Two things give this one away in silhouette: the curved magazine sticking out
; of the LEFT side of the receiver rather than hanging underneath, and the
; straight stock running in line with the bore, which is why the sights stand
; so tall -- the eye sits well above the barrel.
